# Everything in FPMS-OS ends up on a Linux rootfs. Force LF regardless of the
# platform it is authored on.
#
# This is not cosmetic. These files are checked out on a Windows workstation,
# where git's autocrlf would rewrite them to CRLF, and then copied verbatim into
# the image overlay. A shell script whose shebang line ends "\r" fails at exec
# with:
#
#     /usr/local/bin/fpms-wait-net: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter:
#     No such file or directory
#
# which is a spectacularly misleading message - /usr/bin/env plainly exists, and
# the script looks perfect in every editor.
#
# fpms-wait-net is an ExecStartPre= with no "-" prefix on fpms-lidar-ros and
# fpms-tf, so that failure would silently stop the LiDAR and the whole TF tree
# from ever starting. A systemd unit with a CRLF ExecStart, and an /etc/fpms/
# config.env whose values all end in an invisible \r, fail in similarly
# baffling ways.
*               text eol=lf
*.png           binary
*.pgm           binary
*.img           binary
*.rknn          binary
